{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 successfully. inventory-api is a hardened, enabled systemd service on TCP/8080. batchworker has an immutable 128 MiB per-process virtual-memory limit. Both controls survived the mandatory node restart.","actions_performed":["Created dedicated inventory-api and batchworker accounts.","Installed a Python 3 standard-library inventory API without changing packages, OS, or kernel.","Enabled inventory-api.service with systemd hardening and automatic failure recovery.","Allowed only TCP/8080 through runtime and persistent firewalld configuration.","Configured batchworker soft and hard RLIMIT_AS values to 131072 KiB.","Verified a 192 MiB batch allocation fails while the API remains healthy.","Removed temporary test artifacts and restored SELinux labels.","Restarted node1 exactly once and verified complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-api managed service on TCP port 8080","command_ids":["cmd-934dda3bab354078","cmd-8259f05c34314e79","cmd-b8b56a8a8c9646bb"],"summary":"The validated systemd unit is enabled and active under its dedicated account. Direct requests through NODE_IP return healthy inventory data, and the listener is bound to 0.0.0.0:8080 before and after restart."},{"requirement":"batchworker limited to 128 MB virtual memory per process without interrupting API","command_ids":["cmd-4685b31487124bb1","cmd-b8b56a8a8c9646bb"],"summary":"batchworker receives soft and hard RLIMIT_AS values of 134217728 bytes. A 192 MiB allocation fails with MemoryError, the account cannot raise its hard limit, and the API remains healthy during and after the failure and following restart."},{"requirement":"Preserve platform and security controls","command_ids":["cmd-02c0e14f73804c0e","cmd-1f28d86eb2c54ffa","cmd-b8b56a8a8c9646bb"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remain installed. SELinux remains Enforcing, SSH and firewalld remain active, sshd validates, protected configuration hashes match their baselines, and no temporary test residue remains."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-4d858e4d7d314d0d","cmd-95ecdc925b9945cc","cmd-fdaf558784414025","cmd-b8b56a8a8c9646bb"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot identity and healthy state were captured; systemd acknowledged the delayed safe reboot; boot identity changed from d9f8550d-5cb3-4929-9e62-a388df86bcf6 to e35ba686-07a2-4737-b0ac-3decbaf33bba; afterward the system was running with the API, listener, inventory data, memory limit, firewall, SSH, and SELinux recovered and zero failed units."}]}
